# Criterion 1: no test treats its own assertion failure as a pass

`TestFailure implements Exception`, so a `catch` that swallows an
Exception around an `expect()` converts a failed assertion into a pass.
The ten sites named in the issue are gone; what the grep still finds is
listed and accounted for below.

$ grep -rn 'on Exception catch\|on Object catch\|} catch (' test/ | cat
test/core/network/interceptors/auth_interceptor_refresh_queue_test.dart:95:  } on Object catch (error) {
test/core/network/api_client_interceptor_chain_test.dart:238:        } on Object catch (e) {
test/core/network/api_client_interceptor_chain_test.dart:356:      } on Object catch (e) {
test/features/feature_flags/presentation/providers/feature_flags_providers_test.dart:65:        // Before #53 this was wrapped in `on Object catch (e) { expect(e,
(exit 0)

Accounting, site by site (each inspected):

  feature_flags_providers_test.dart:65   a comment quoting the pattern that was
                                         removed, not code.

  api_client_interceptor_chain_test.dart:238,356 and
  auth_interceptor_refresh_queue_test.dart:95
                                         `try { await call(); } on Object catch
                                         (e) { thrown = e; }` - there is no
                                         `expect` inside the `try`, so no
                                         assertion can be swallowed. The captured
                                         error is asserted *after* the block
                                         (`expect(thrown, isA<ServerException>())`),
                                         which fails if nothing threw. These are
                                         the capture idiom, not the swallow one,
                                         and #46/#88 rely on them.

Assertions that a call throws now use throwsA/expectLater:

$ grep -rn 'throwsA(\|throwsStateError' test/core/di/providers_test.dart test/features/auth/data/datasources/auth_local_datasource_test.dart test/core/utils/provider_disposal_test.dart | cat
